    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. u said the ABCDE signs are 'classic' for light skin, but the other one sounds way more vague. like, if i'm in a clinic and i see a patient with dark skin, is there a specific way the cancer actually looks or behaves differently biologically, or is it just harder to see because of the pigment? sometimes i feel like the textbooks just gloss over it without giving real clinical markers.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
