      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While camouflage due to background pigmentation is a major challenge, there are specific biological considerations. Melanoma in darker skin sometimes exhibits greater vertical growth, appearing more as a nodule rather than a flat patch, which can be an important visual clue. Biologically, some studies suggest melanomas on darker skin may have different metastatic pathways or growth patterns, though this is still an area of active research. Ultimately, clinical vigilance for any new or changing pigmented lesion is the most critical takeaway for diagnosis across all skin tones.",
